{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From Gerar the king rides [C]out to the [Dm]field
With [Bb]Phicol, the comman[C]der, standing [F]by
He [Gm]speaks to the pa[C]triarch, [Dm]voice low and [Bb]mild
[Gm]God is with you in [C]everything you [Dm]do, he said
Swear to me here [C]by the God of high [Dm]heaven
That [Bb]you will not deal [C]falsely with my [F]line
[Gm]I will show you kind[C]ness, [Dm]as [C]you have shown [Bb]me
[Gm]In the land where [C]you have stayed as a [Dm]stranger
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Phicol the commander of [C]the army [Bb]stands
Witness to the oath, [C]the covenant in [Dm]hands
Seven ewe lambs set [C]apart from the flock
[Bb]Accept these as [C]my witness that [Dm]I dug this well
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Abraham takes [C]sheep and cattle to [Dm]give
The [Bb]two of them make a [C]covenant of [F]peace
He [Gm]sets apart [C]seven ewe [C]lambs to [Bb]live
As [Gm]proof that he [C]dug the well in this [Dm]place
The place is [C]called Beershe[Dm]ba, they swear
[Bb]When they had made the [C]covenant at [F]Beersheba
[Gm]Abimelech [C]and Phicol the [Dm]com[C]mander set [Bb]out
Re[Gm]turned to the land [C]of the Philis[Dm]tines, true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Phicol the commander of the [C]army stands
[Bb]Witness to the oath, the [C]covenant in hands
[Dm]Seven ewe lambs set a[C]part from the flock
Ac[Bb]cept these as my [C]witness that I [Dm]dug this well
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Years pass and I[C]saac lives in the [Dm]same land
[Bb]Abimelech comes [C]again from [F]the city gate
With [Gm]Ahuzzath the ad[C]viser, [Dm]and [C]Phicol in [Bb]hand
They [Gm]saw clearly that the Lord [C]was with you, [Dm]said they
Isaac asks why [C]they have come to his [Dm]door
[Bb]Since they hated him and [C]sent him away from [F]you
They [Gm]seek a sworn agree[C]ment, [Dm]peace [C]between [Bb]us
Just [Gm]as we did you [C]nothing but good and [Dm]sent you away
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
He makes them a feast, [C]they eat and [Dm]drink
[Bb]Early in the morn[C]ing they rise and [F]swear
Ex[Gm]changing oaths with [C]one another, [Dm]plain [C]
[Bb]Then [Gm]Isaac sends them off, [C]they leave him in [Dm]peace
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Phicol the commander of [C]the army [Bb]stands
Witness to the oath, [C]the covenant in [Dm][C]hands
{end_of_verse}

